WEBVTT

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:09.110
Sangre y Fuego!

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:14.830
Guy, you coward.

00:00:15.370 --> 00:00:16.950
How dare you use a bomb.

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:18.920
I thought we were goners.

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:23.790
He took all 3,000 automata down with him.

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:25.590
What do we do now?

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:27.840
We chase the train. Anybody alive?

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:29.760
Any survivors?

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:34.930
Yes, right here.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:36.640
Good, it's you.

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:39.640
Go, stop that train!

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:55.700
Am I destined to lose my way?

00:00:55.870 --> 00:00:58.870
All I want is to have fun in my life

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:05.090
All I want is to be with those I love

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:11.340
Ready or not
Here I come

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:14.220
I don't care anymore

00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:17.010
I just don't know anymore

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:20.560
I wish everything would just disappear

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:23.690
There are days when I think like that

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:26.610
But everything is precious to me

00:01:26.770 --> 00:01:29.440
And so I fight on

00:01:29.650 --> 00:01:32.950
Today was a tough day

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:36.200
I almost gave up hope

00:01:36.370 --> 00:01:42.080
But the truth is I don't want
to lose anything anymore

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:45.750
I wish everything would just disappear

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:48.960
There are days when I think like that

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:51.760
But everything is precious to me

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:54.800
And so I must fight

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:12.990
#31 Black shooting star

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:19.410
Listen up.
The curtains have finally been raised.

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:26.460
The show is about taking the space shuttle
on this puffer train to the end of Russia.

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:28.670
There's no pay, no rehearsal.

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:30.500
And we've only got one shot.

00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:33.050
But we gotta do it.

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:39.600
Because if we mess up, there won't be
anyone left to come see our circus.

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:41.970
Not a single person.

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:44.640
So, let's do this.

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:49.730
And after we reach the launch pad.

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:52.030
Big guy. You take it from there.

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:54.860
I don't know much about you.

00:02:55.150 --> 00:03:00.030
But Fou relies on you, and he knows best.
We're counting on you.

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:02.290
Leave it to me.

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:08.830
Gather around. Want something that'll make
automata stop dead in their tracks?

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:11.420
Vilma's special knives. Come get 'em.

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:13.920
What? You mean that?

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:19.470
I heard from Fou that your blood
is really poisonous for automata.

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:22.430
Well, yes.

00:03:22.890 --> 00:03:24.770
And I remembered.

00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:28.520
About when you and I fought.

00:03:29.690 --> 00:03:35.610
I had these checked, and these knives
had a bit of your blood left on them.

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:37.610
Thanks.

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:40.700
We can give them
a taste of their own medicine.

00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:44.250
But why is Shirogane's blood
on so many knives?

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:47.080
That's a little secret. Right?

00:03:49.210 --> 00:03:53.090
Okay, big guy and Shirogane
go up to the first car.

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:57.010
We should split up
so they can't attack us all at once.

00:03:57.470 --> 00:04:02.010
Hold on, I'm going to fight with you.
Why do I have to be with her?

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:05.350
He's right. Why just us?

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:08.020
I've fought automata for a long time.

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:10.190
How dense can you get?

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:14.360
You're going up on that space shuttle
to the space station.

00:04:14.530 --> 00:04:16.650
Well yeah, but I...

00:04:16.820 --> 00:04:20.110
What, are you saying
you're stronger than us?

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:21.660
You're so special, huh?

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:23.450
No, of course not.

00:04:23.660 --> 00:04:27.830
Then leave this to us
and save your energy for later.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:30.920
You need to learn how to fly
the space shuttle, too.

00:04:32.130 --> 00:04:35.210
Shirogane, you've got a point.

00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:38.970
You're the most experienced in
fighting those automata.

00:04:39.260 --> 00:04:43.430
And that's why you're going with him.
You're the strongest.

00:04:43.890 --> 00:04:44.760
Protect him.

00:04:45.470 --> 00:04:50.390
Damn it, I don't want to put her
in the same room as that bear guy either.

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:53.270
I wish she'd fight alongside us.

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:54.650
But jeez...

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:56.900
Guess it can't be helped.

00:04:57.690 --> 00:05:01.910
Why not? You can come back to fight
if something comes up.

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:06.660
Until then, go spend your last moments
with the man you love.

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:08.080
Vilma!

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:11.620
Go on.

00:05:12.880 --> 00:05:13.670
Okay.

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:18.760
We'll be going then.

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:21.800
Call us if anything happens.

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:27.220
As if we ever would.

00:05:27.390 --> 00:05:29.560
That naive little girl.

00:05:29.730 --> 00:05:35.400
"Nouveaux enfants de la balle," people
born outside the circus are so gullible.

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:41.820
Fine, you want to stay
with Shirogane, right?

00:05:42.280 --> 00:05:44.410
Go on to the second car.

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:55.000
Chin up, Master.

00:05:55.170 --> 00:05:58.500
We're gonna reach the train
to protect Shirogane, right?

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:00.670
Yeah, but...

00:06:01.670 --> 00:06:02.800
Guy...

00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:10.680
That handsome man played out his role.

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:13.020
Yeah, you're right.

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:14.560
So...

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:22.780
Guess we're faster than
this brat's puppet, eh Anoss?

00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:27.910
Yeah, Keniss.
Even with the heavy loads we're carrying.

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:31.200
How rude, referring to a lady's weight.

00:06:31.370 --> 00:06:33.080
Oops, sorry.

00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:35.170
There were survivors!

00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:36.830
We can't let them go.

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:38.460
Too bad.

00:06:38.630 --> 00:06:43.380
Wild West Jane is always first to arrive,
just like a bullet.

00:06:46.970 --> 00:06:48.350
You're one lucky brat.

00:06:48.510 --> 00:06:51.930
I'm in a hurry. I'll shoot you down later.

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:58.690
Now, Anoss. Your job is to take me
to the train.

00:06:59.060 --> 00:07:00.480
Stop fooling around.

00:07:00.650 --> 00:07:04.110
Well of course, Lady Spider.

00:07:04.280 --> 00:07:06.660
It won't take but a second.

00:07:07.240 --> 00:07:09.280
Not so fast!

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:17.250
That idiot, he never listens.

00:07:30.760 --> 00:07:32.350
You look happy.

00:07:32.510 --> 00:07:36.190
We could be attacked any minute now.
Aren't you scared?

00:07:36.350 --> 00:07:37.480
Scared?

00:07:39.770 --> 00:07:42.730
Only memories are capable of
really scaring me.

00:07:43.530 --> 00:07:47.910
They keep replaying, over and over.
My deepest regrets.

00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:52.280
But anyway.

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:57.290
Have I ever told you
that I come from a railroad circus?

00:07:57.750 --> 00:08:02.540
You mean, your circus traveled
around the country on a train?

00:08:02.710 --> 00:08:03.550
Right.

00:08:04.420 --> 00:08:07.970
I was born to a family of knife throwers.

00:08:09.180 --> 00:08:10.890
With one little brother.

00:08:11.890 --> 00:08:13.720
So you're of royal circus blood.

00:08:14.060 --> 00:08:18.810
I ended up choosing a job
other than the circus for myself.

00:08:19.270 --> 00:08:22.820
But ever since I joined
Nakamachi Circus...

00:08:26.690 --> 00:08:28.320
It's been such fun.

00:08:28.860 --> 00:08:32.030
I got to meet you all and Shirogane.

00:08:32.490 --> 00:08:36.080
And here I am, on a train,
as a member of a circus.

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:39.080
It was a dream of mine.

00:08:40.290 --> 00:08:43.340
To be in a circus like this
with my little brother.

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:48.170
You never know where life takes you.

00:08:48.340 --> 00:08:51.010
My brother and I were abandoned as kids.

00:08:51.550 --> 00:08:52.470
Abandoned?

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:53.850
Yeah.

00:08:55.100 --> 00:08:58.480
An orphanage we knew of
had their hands full.

00:08:58.640 --> 00:09:00.600
So my wife took these two in.

00:09:03.020 --> 00:09:04.610
You had a wife.

00:09:05.650 --> 00:09:10.110
A circus is a tight-knit community.

00:09:10.700 --> 00:09:14.410
It's like a lot of families
traveling together.

00:09:15.120 --> 00:09:17.870
So it was no big deal taking these two in.

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:22.290
But they had a hard time
opening their hearts to Fusae.

00:09:22.710 --> 00:09:26.960
Hiro didn't eat the rice balls
Mom made for us.

00:09:27.130 --> 00:09:31.220
Nori went and sold the clothes
she made for us.

00:09:31.970 --> 00:09:34.220
Well, you know.

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:39.140
It felt awkward. And it was like
we'd been kidnapped by the circus.

00:09:39.350 --> 00:09:43.940
Yeah, I thought Mom was just acting nice
to try to fool us.

00:09:44.350 --> 00:09:46.650
But you made up with her, right?

00:09:46.860 --> 00:09:50.030
-Yeah!
-We sure did. I was faster.

00:09:50.190 --> 00:09:52.490
No way, I made up with her first.

00:09:52.650 --> 00:09:54.280
-What did you say?
-You little...

00:09:55.120 --> 00:09:59.830
Back then, the circus drew large crowds,
and we made good money.

00:10:02.290 --> 00:10:04.630
Fusae was into pottery.

00:10:04.790 --> 00:10:08.590
She treasured a vase
that cost quite a fortune.

00:10:10.760 --> 00:10:13.630
I was scared out of my wits.

00:10:14.130 --> 00:10:18.180
I knew I'd never be able to pay it off
no matter how hard I worked.

00:10:22.350 --> 00:10:24.560
I thought my only choice was to run.

00:10:25.400 --> 00:10:26.230
But...

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:28.820
Why are you running away?

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:30.320
Silly boy!

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:36.070
Things break.

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:38.700
When they do, we can just buy another.

00:10:39.450 --> 00:10:42.080
But not you, Hiro.

00:10:43.870 --> 00:10:44.870
You...

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:49.840
Nothing could ever replace you.

00:11:05.230 --> 00:11:10.570
That's when I finally realized
that this woman was my mother.

00:11:12.650 --> 00:11:15.280
With Nori, it was marbles.

00:11:15.450 --> 00:11:16.570
Marbles?

00:11:17.110 --> 00:11:18.990
There's a game Japanese kids play.

00:11:19.160 --> 00:11:22.910
Our teacher taught it to the class,
and everyone played it.

00:11:24.290 --> 00:11:25.910
But I was awful at it.

00:11:26.370 --> 00:11:29.920
I kept losing,
and the other kids made fun of me.

00:11:30.380 --> 00:11:32.670
All right, let's train!

00:11:34.130 --> 00:11:35.840
She was so serious about it.

00:11:36.220 --> 00:11:38.760
She didn't even change out of her costume.

00:11:40.640 --> 00:11:44.430
We practiced every day.
She really meant it.

00:11:47.390 --> 00:11:48.900
Don't force it.

00:11:49.060 --> 00:11:52.820
Once you learn to spin it,
you'll be invincible.

00:11:55.030 --> 00:12:00.620
By that time,
she was the only mother to me.

00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:08.580
I came home one day after winning a game,
and she was just as happy as I was.

00:12:12.130 --> 00:12:16.300
I'm sure your mother had her reasons.

00:12:16.800 --> 00:12:19.800
So you don't have to call me "Mom."

00:12:20.930 --> 00:12:24.640
Your real mom is sure to come for you
someday soon.

00:12:25.470 --> 00:12:27.310
Mom always said that.

00:12:27.770 --> 00:12:32.400
But she used to get so happy
whenever we called her "Mom."

00:12:34.360 --> 00:12:38.950
If you like to be called "Mom" so much,
why don't you just ask them to?

00:12:39.820 --> 00:12:44.120
No, they didn't join this circus
because they wanted to.

00:12:44.790 --> 00:12:48.210
When somebody comes for them,
they're free to leave.

00:12:51.750 --> 00:12:57.510
And when that day comes,
I don't want to hear them say, "Bye, Mom."

00:12:58.880 --> 00:13:00.300
It'd hurt too much.

00:13:02.590 --> 00:13:07.350
Fusae was more of a mother to them
than anybody else ever could be.

00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:11.520
Until that day...

00:13:17.610 --> 00:13:19.110
Mom, you have a fever?

00:13:19.530 --> 00:13:21.490
You should sit out today.

00:13:21.660 --> 00:13:27.200
Of course not. Fevers are nothing
for entertainers once we're out on stage.

00:13:31.290 --> 00:13:33.210
She was so beautiful.

00:13:34.080 --> 00:13:37.210
Like a goddess
straight out of a picture book.

00:13:52.940 --> 00:13:54.860
The crowd was bewildered.

00:13:55.810 --> 00:13:58.440
We ran towards Fusae. And she said...

00:14:00.280 --> 00:14:03.450
Hurry, carry me out.

00:14:05.570 --> 00:14:08.200
The audience will worry.

00:14:09.660 --> 00:14:10.750
Dear...

00:14:12.210 --> 00:14:14.620
Start the next act. Hurry.

00:14:16.540 --> 00:14:18.130
Carefully, easy now.

00:14:18.300 --> 00:14:20.380
Hiro, Nori, come back.

00:14:20.550 --> 00:14:22.720
No, we're going with Mom!

00:14:22.880 --> 00:14:24.180
We're staying with Mom!

00:14:24.930 --> 00:14:25.890
No.

00:14:26.800 --> 00:14:31.020
You two still have the unicycle act
for the finale left.

00:14:31.220 --> 00:14:32.230
But...

00:14:33.020 --> 00:14:34.350
The circus...

00:14:35.730 --> 00:14:36.900
must never...

00:14:38.230 --> 00:14:40.230
stop the show...

00:14:41.280 --> 00:14:42.690
Mom!

00:14:43.200 --> 00:14:44.570
Mom...

00:14:46.950 --> 00:14:48.950
"Mom," huh?

00:14:51.450 --> 00:14:53.120
When I come back...

00:14:54.370 --> 00:14:57.580
maybe I really will become your mom.

00:15:00.750 --> 00:15:05.680
Mom never came back.

00:15:06.470 --> 00:15:08.510
What a kind woman she was.

00:15:08.970 --> 00:15:11.470
So, how's your little brother?

00:15:12.470 --> 00:15:15.690
You're going to
put on a circus together, right?

00:15:15.850 --> 00:15:18.480
Sorry, but my story is the same as yours.

00:15:18.650 --> 00:15:20.360
He's already passed away.

00:15:21.730 --> 00:15:22.780
I see.

00:15:24.030 --> 00:15:26.700
Enough looking back. We have guests.

00:15:34.120 --> 00:15:35.370
Found it.

00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:39.040
I'm Wild West Jane,
a champion with a rifle.

00:15:39.670 --> 00:15:43.170
But I'm even better at throwing knives.

00:15:43.800 --> 00:15:47.180
And spreading ZONAPHA throughout America.

00:15:47.930 --> 00:15:48.890
What...?

00:15:49.800 --> 00:15:54.310
Seems like this villain is
my personal archenemy.

00:15:57.980 --> 00:16:02.690
I used to shoot ZONAPHA bullets
up and down the country with these guns.

00:16:07.490 --> 00:16:09.990
You're not the only one with firearms.

00:16:12.660 --> 00:16:17.540
So you were the one
who did that to my hometown!

00:16:19.250 --> 00:16:21.210
Ladies and gentlemen.

00:16:21.500 --> 00:16:25.210
The reincarnation of a knife master
from the great pioneer days.

00:16:25.670 --> 00:16:29.130
Black Vilma!

00:16:31.090 --> 00:16:33.470
Amazing! You're so great, Sis.

00:16:33.640 --> 00:16:35.100
You bet I am.

00:16:37.230 --> 00:16:38.690
I have bad news.

00:16:39.270 --> 00:16:42.900
Jim has contracted a rare disease
called ZONAPHA syndrome.

00:16:45.820 --> 00:16:47.610
You bastard!

00:16:47.900 --> 00:16:50.780
Why, you're quite worked up.

00:16:50.990 --> 00:16:54.910
Yeah, seeing your face
has made me go a bit crazy.

00:16:57.500 --> 00:16:59.460
She really has gone crazy!

00:17:00.080 --> 00:17:02.290
I understand what this journey is for now.

00:17:02.460 --> 00:17:06.510
It's to defeat you. To avenge Jim.

00:17:07.050 --> 00:17:09.510
I will never forgive you.

00:17:11.130 --> 00:17:14.470
I heard you changed jobs again.

00:17:14.680 --> 00:17:19.520
Yeah, but this new job pays really well.

00:17:20.190 --> 00:17:24.190
My treatments cost a lot of money, huh?
I'm sorry.

00:17:24.360 --> 00:17:26.860
That's none of your business now.

00:17:27.030 --> 00:17:29.030
You just work on getting better.

00:17:31.030 --> 00:17:34.740
We're gonna do
that knife show together, right?

00:17:35.450 --> 00:17:40.250
That's right.
We were supposed to do it together, Jim.

00:17:52.840 --> 00:17:54.180
One down.

00:17:54.340 --> 00:17:57.260
No-one can outshoot our Jane.

00:18:02.060 --> 00:18:03.020
Jim...

00:18:04.400 --> 00:18:06.060
When I get better...

00:18:08.070 --> 00:18:10.610
You said we'd do a show together.

00:18:11.740 --> 00:18:16.280
Jim and Vilma's Wild West Knife Show.

00:18:17.530 --> 00:18:18.540
Don't worry.

00:18:20.120 --> 00:18:21.960
Black Vilma's Shooting Stars...

00:18:23.120 --> 00:18:25.000
Are faster than a bullet.

00:18:32.090 --> 00:18:33.760
Jim!

00:18:45.270 --> 00:18:49.230
Our show, with the two of us.

00:18:50.150 --> 00:18:51.690
It would've drawn crowds.

00:18:55.950 --> 00:19:00.200
You can't rely on guns.

00:19:01.200 --> 00:19:04.460
All I need are my knives.

00:19:04.910 --> 00:19:09.170
This half-dead woman still wants to fight.

00:19:09.340 --> 00:19:12.210
Oh dear, in that condition?

00:19:12.670 --> 00:19:15.300
Can I rip her apart then?

00:19:15.470 --> 00:19:17.260
Sure, go ahead.

00:19:20.970 --> 00:19:22.140
Too bad.

00:19:31.690 --> 00:19:32.570
What...?

00:19:33.940 --> 00:19:35.360
What am I...

00:19:36.450 --> 00:19:38.280
What am I doing...?

00:19:40.240 --> 00:19:41.870
It's over now!

00:19:42.990 --> 00:19:45.870
Who is he...?

00:19:46.620 --> 00:19:51.210
There's something I have to do.

00:19:52.380 --> 00:19:54.710
But I can't remember what.

00:19:55.470 --> 00:19:57.340
Die!

00:20:00.390 --> 00:20:01.220
What?

00:20:05.810 --> 00:20:07.600
Let go of me!

00:20:07.810 --> 00:20:08.850
Vilma!

00:20:14.980 --> 00:20:16.240
Jim...

00:20:16.690 --> 00:20:19.490
Oh dear, an interruption.

00:20:19.660 --> 00:20:23.080
Not that it matters.
You're going to die soon.

00:20:23.540 --> 00:20:26.960
I'll just kill that brat afterwards.

00:20:29.080 --> 00:20:30.210
Brat...?

00:20:31.460 --> 00:20:33.340
I won't let you.

00:20:35.300 --> 00:20:37.010
Who are you?

00:20:38.340 --> 00:20:39.760
Get out of my way.

00:20:40.260 --> 00:20:44.010
I have to throw my knife...

00:20:45.680 --> 00:20:49.770
into the apple on Jim's head!

00:20:49.980 --> 00:20:54.270
You fool!
I told you I'm even better with knives.

00:20:55.940 --> 00:20:57.030
Please God.

00:20:58.740 --> 00:21:00.780
May this knife hit its mark...

00:21:20.180 --> 00:21:23.340
The crowd can't wait to see us, Sis.

00:21:23.510 --> 00:21:28.430
All right, let's get
Jim and Vilma's Knife Show started.

00:21:32.190 --> 00:21:36.270
That's right.
Black Vilma's Shooting Stars...

00:21:41.530 --> 00:21:43.450
Are faster...

00:21:44.450 --> 00:21:46.160
than a bullet...

00:21:48.200 --> 00:21:50.410
Pathetic weakling humans!

00:22:04.470 --> 00:22:05.550
Vilma!

00:22:06.260 --> 00:22:08.350
Vilma...!

00:22:20.740 --> 00:22:25.200
A past that can't become a memory
plays on repeat

00:22:25.410 --> 00:22:30.120
In my mind is a forgotten thing
that I still remember

00:22:30.290 --> 00:22:34.790
Questions remain unanswered
but I must go now

00:22:34.960 --> 00:22:39.670
I walk in the dark,
making a promise to my footprints

00:22:39.840 --> 00:22:44.380
So many similar beings
leading similar lives

00:22:44.550 --> 00:22:49.100
Was there a reason
for me to be born at all?

00:22:49.260 --> 00:22:53.810
The world lost all sound
but for the ticking of a clock

00:22:53.980 --> 00:22:58.650
A missing heart keeps shouting

00:22:58.820 --> 00:23:03.440
A meaningless life was shaking

00:23:03.610 --> 00:23:08.160
All because of your unique existence

00:23:08.320 --> 00:23:12.790
If the reason for the pain
is revealed someday

00:23:13.160 --> 00:23:17.540
If you find a home
for those tears someday

00:23:17.960 --> 00:23:22.630
You shall sleep
with the whole universe in your arms

00:23:22.800 --> 00:23:30.510
I know it still plays in your heart

00:23:30.850 --> 00:23:34.520
The melody that brought you here
